# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Manufacturer material — never published.
#
# Vendor schematics are submitted in confidence and describe unreleased
# hardware; the config.h files generated from them describe the same boards.
# Both stay local. Keep it that way even though the repo is private.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pdf
*.PDF
configs/
config.h
out/

# Generated extraction output
*_SCH.md
*_SCH.json

# mcu-parser/data/firmware.json IS committed, deliberately. It is generated by
# seed_firmware.py from a Betaflight tree, but without it a clone cannot convert
# anything at all - which rules out handing this to anyone who does not already
# keep a firmware checkout. It carries no confidential material: every byte is
# harvested from Betaflight's own GPL sources, and the seeder records the rev,
# branch and date but deliberately not the path it was generated from.
#
# It goes stale on its own, silently, so tests/check_seed_drift.py runs in CI
# against Betaflight master and fails when the tables move.

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
uv.lock

# schematic-extractor is its own git repository (independently versioned)
/schematic-extractor/
build/
